{"type": "root", "attrs": {"type": "node", "context": "cop2", "internal": "light", "icon": "COP2/light", "index": "no", "version": null, "namespace": null}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lighting"], "extent": [74, 87]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Adds a light to the image."], "extent": [87, 122]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This operator adds a light to the image. The light can be directional or\nnon, and have ambient, specular and diffuse components. The image can be\na flat image, an image with a bump map, or a deep raster image\ncontaining point and/or normal planes."], "extent": [165, 414]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Flat Lighting"], "extent": [414, 434], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Flat lighting requires no extra information. It assumes the image is\n    a flat plane, and applies the lighting equation to the pixels. The\n    image occupies the area (0,0,0) to (1,1,0)."], "extent": [434, 628]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The light position should have a positive Z value. The center of the\n    image is (0.5, 0.5, 0). The distance the light is from Z=0\n    determines the brightness and the light\u2019s shape (if a cone line is\n    used)."], "extent": [628, 847]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Bump Map Lighting"], "extent": [847, 871], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Bump Map lighting requires a bump map, which can be produced with\n    the Bump COP. This type of lighting is similar to Flat lighting,\n    except that the surface normals are perturbed based on the bump\n    map."], "extent": [871, 1089]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["To adjust the height of the bumps, you will need to brighten or dim\n    the bump map with a Bright COP. Or, if the bump map was created with\n    the Bump COP, adjust the Bump Height parameter there."], "extent": [1089, 1293]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Deep Raster (3D) Lighting"], "extent": [1293, 1325], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["3D lighting can be done with the help of Point and Normal maps,\n    which can be generated from the Deep Raster tab of the Mantra ROP.\n    If only a Point map is present, the Lighting COP will attempt to\n    build normals from the point positions. If only a Normal map is\n    present, the process is similar to that of Bump Map lighting, and\n    the points are assumed to be in the range (0,0,0) to (1,1,0)."], "extent": [1325, 1739]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The light can be placed anywhere relative to the 3D points. It is\n    useful to use the viewport inspect function (", {"keys": ["i"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, ") to determine the\n    3D point values so the light can be positioned more accurately."], "extent": [1739, 1951]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Volumetric Lighting"], "extent": [1951, 1977], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Volumetric lighting can be used with any of the above lighting\n    techniques, though it is most effective when used with 3D lighting.\n    Volumetric lighting adds an atmospheric light-scattering effect so\n    that the cone of light can be seen."], "extent": [1977, 2229]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Since volumetric lighting is quite time consuming to compute, it is\n    a good idea to get all your other lighting parameters setup first,\n    and then enable this option."], "extent": [2229, 2406]}]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["If the alpha plane is scoped, the amount of light at each point is placed\nin it."], "extent": [2406, 2488]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Overloading VEX Parameters"], "extent": [27, 60], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This operator is implemented in VEX, which supports parameter\noverloading. If the first input has a plane which matches an\noperation parameter\u2019s channel name, the input plane will be used as\nthe parameter\u2019s value, effectively overriding it. The overloaded\nparameter is then evaluated from the plane on a per-pixel basis."], "extent": [60, 383]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "em", "text": ["eg."]}, " If the input COP has the following planes:"], "extent": [383, 433]}, {"lang": null, "type": "pre", "indent": 0, "text": ["\nC{r,g,b}\nA\nfogdens\n"], "extent": [433, 460]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["and it is fed into a VEX Fog COP, the fog density will be determined\nat each pixel by the fogdens plane, since the Fog Density\nparameter\u2019s channel name matches the 'fogdens' channel name."], "extent": [460, 649]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Scoping"], "extent": [57, 75], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This operation may be restricted to certain planes, or\n        components of planes. In addition, the operation may be applied\n        to a subset of frames within the sequence. An image must have\n        both its frame and plane scoped to be modified."], "extent": [75, 338]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Images that are not modified are passed through, which does not\n        take any memory or processing time."], "extent": [338, 455]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Masking"], "extent": [56, 74], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This operation may be masked, which restricts the operation to\n        an area of the image. The mask may be inverted, brightened or\n        dimmed."], "extent": [74, 233]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The mask input is on the side of the node. The label on the\n        connector indicates the plane being used as a mask."], "extent": [233, 362]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The mask input can also be scaled to fit the output image\u2019s resolution, if they differ. If this node is changing constantly, and the mask is not, it is somewhat faster to put a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/scale", "type": "link", "text": ["Scale COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/scale.html"}, " down to do the resize for the mask image. Otherwise, the scale will occur every time this node cooks."], "extent": [362, 678]}]}, {"level": 1, "id": "parameters", "container": true, "type": "parameters_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [2592, 2604], "body": [{"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Lighting"], "extent": [2604, 2624], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Surface Type"], "extent": [2624, 2647], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Specifies the type of surface lighting to use:"], "extent": [2647, 2707]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Flat"], "extent": [2707, 2725], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Image has uniform normals and uniform depth."], "extent": [2725, 2786]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Bump Map"], "extent": [2786, 2808], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Image has bumped normals and uniform depth."], "extent": [2808, 2868]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Point & Normal"], "extent": [2868, 2896], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Image has normal & point maps for 3D lighting."], "extent": [2896, 2959]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Point Only"], "extent": [2959, 2983], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Image has a point map for pseudo-3D lighting."], "extent": [2983, 3045]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Normal Map"], "extent": [3045, 3069], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Image has uniform depth and varying normals."], "extent": [3069, 3130]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Eye Distance"], "extent": [3130, 3152], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The distance from the eye to the image (at Z=0)."], "extent": [3189, 3250]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/eyedistance"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Ambient"], "extent": [3250, 3267], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The ambient component of the light."], "extent": [3327, 3375]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/ambcolr /ambcolg /ambcolb /ambcola"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Diffuse"], "extent": [3375, 3392], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The diffuse component of the light."], "extent": [3464, 3512]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/lightdiffr /lightdiffg /lightdiffb /lightdiffa"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Specular"], "extent": [3512, 3530], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The specular component of the light."], "extent": [3602, 3651]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/lightspecr /lightspecg /lightspecb /lightspeca"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Correct for Aspect Ratio"], "extent": [3651, 3685], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If the image is not square, this adjusts the coordinates so\n            that spotlights are still circular."], "extent": [3685, 3805]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Color Operation"], "extent": [3805, 3830], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["How to apply the light to the existing image:"], "extent": [3830, 3889]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Light Existing Color"], "extent": [3889, 3923], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["The image color is used as the color of the surface,\n                and the lighting calculation replaces it."], "extent": [3923, 4050]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Add to Existing Color"], "extent": [4050, 4085], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 20, "text": ["The image color is used as the color of the surface,"], "extent": [4085, 4158]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["and the lighting calculation is added to it."], "extent": [4158, 4219]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["New Lighting Only"], "extent": [4219, 4250], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["The image color is ignored, and replaced by the\n                new lighting. This will show only the ambient, diffuse\n                and specular colors."], "extent": [4250, 4423]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Material"], "extent": [4423, 4442], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["This tab allows you to change the diffuse and specular models."], "extent": [4442, 4515]}, {"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Diffuse Model"], "extent": [4515, 4538], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The type of diffuse model to use:"], "extent": [4538, 4585]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Simple"], "extent": [4585, 4605], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Simple dot product model."], "extent": [4605, 4647]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Oren-Nayar"], "extent": [4647, 4671], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Rougher material model, like clay."], "extent": [4671, 4722]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Diffuse Roughness"], "extent": [4722, 4749], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The roughness for the Oren-Nayar model."], "extent": [4784, 4836]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/diffrough"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Specular Model"], "extent": [4836, 4860], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The specular model to use, Phong or Blinn."], "extent": [4860, 4915]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Exponent"], "extent": [4915, 4933], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The Phong specular exponent."], "extent": [4966, 5007]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/specexp"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Roughness"], "extent": [5007, 5026], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The Blinn roughness parameter."], "extent": [5061, 5105]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/specrough"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Light"], "extent": [5105, 5121], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Light position and orientation."], "extent": [5121, 5163]}, {"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Position"], "extent": [5163, 5181], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The position of the light. In Flat, Bump Map and Normal Map\n            modes, the image coordinates are {0,0,0} (bottom left) to\n            {1,1,0} (top right)."], "extent": [5238, 5413]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/lightpos1 /lightpos2 /lightpos3"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Attenuation"], "extent": [5413, 5434], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The distance at which the light is at 50% intensity."], "extent": [5465, 5530]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/atten"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Directional Light"], "extent": [5530, 5557], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If on, the light is directional."], "extent": [5557, 5602]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Direction"], "extent": [5602, 5621], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The direction vector of the light."], "extent": [5681, 5728]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/direction1 /direction2 /direction3"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Cone"], "extent": [5728, 5742], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The cone size of the light, in degrees."], "extent": [5777, 5829]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/coneangle"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Cone Falloff"], "extent": [5829, 5851], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The falloff cone size of the light, in degrees."], "extent": [5886, 5946]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/fallangle"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Falloff"], "extent": [5946, 5963], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The falloff function for the light."], "extent": [5963, 6012]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Volumetric"], "extent": [6012, 6033], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Adds volumetric light effects. Takes quite a bit longer to\n        compute."], "extent": [6033, 6119]}, {"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Atmosphere Scatter"], "extent": [6119, 6147], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The amount of light scatter the atmosphere causes. Higher\n            numbers produce foggier lights."], "extent": [6183, 6297]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/atmosphere"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Light Falloff"], "extent": [6297, 6320], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The distance that the volumetric fog extends away from the\n            light."], "extent": [6356, 6446]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/atfalldist"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Falloff Function"], "extent": [6446, 6472], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The volumetric fog falloff function."], "extent": [6472, 6521]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Light Core Size"], "extent": [6521, 6546], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Increases or decreases the light hotspot size."], "extent": [6577, 6636]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/lsize"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Ray March Step"], "extent": [6636, 6660], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The step size when marching through the light volume.\n            Smaller values produce finer results at the expense of\n            computation time."], "extent": [6696, 6860]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/atmos_step"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Planes"], "extent": [6860, 6877], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Bump, Point Normal Planes in 2nd input"], "extent": [6877, 6926], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If on, all the specified planes are in input 2, otherwise\n            they are in input 1."], "extent": [6926, 7029]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Bump, Point, Normal Name"], "extent": [7029, 7063], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The name of the corresponding input planes."], "extent": [7063, 7119]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Mask"], "extent": [706, 722], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["A mask can be chosen to limit the effect of the operator to\n        areas defined by the mask. The mask can be taken from the mask\n        input (side input) or from the first input itself."], "extent": [722, 922]}, {"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Effect Amount"], "extent": [922, 945], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If no mask is present, this blends the output with the input\n            by a constant amount (0 = all input, 1 = all output)."], "extent": [983, 1123]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If a mask is present, this amount multiplies the mask."], "extent": [1123, 1191]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/effectamount"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Operation Mask"], "extent": [1191, 1215], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Selects the mask plane to use as a mask from the mask input.\n            The mask can be selected from:"], "extent": [1261, 1378]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["A mask can be a component of a plane or an entire plane. If\n            a vector plane is supplied as a mask, its components are\n            multiplied by the images' components."], "extent": [1378, 1570]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"type": "strong", "text": ["Scalar Mask ('A', 'C.r')"]}], "extent": [1570, 1610]}, {"lang": null, "type": "pre", "indent": 12, "text": ["\n            C.r = I.r * M\n            C.g = I.g * M\n            C.b = I.b * M\n            \n            "], "extent": [1610, 1733]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"type": "strong", "text": ["Vector Mask ('C')"]}], "extent": [1733, 1766]}, {"lang": null, "type": "pre", "indent": 12, "text": ["\n            C.r = I.r * M.r\n            C.g = I.g * M.g\n            C.b = I.b * M.b\n            \n            "], "extent": [1766, 1895]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["First Input"], "extent": [1895, 1921], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Useful for masking the operation to the image\u2019s own\n                alpha plane."], "extent": [1921, 2018]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Mask Input"], "extent": [2018, 2042], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Selects the mask from the side mask input."], "extent": [2042, 2101]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Off"], "extent": [2101, 2118], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Turns off masking, without requiring disconnection of\n                the mask input (useful for temporarily disabling the\n                mask)."], "extent": [2118, 2280]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/maskinput /maskplane"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Resize Mask to Fit Image"], "extent": [2280, 2314], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If the mask image is a different resolution than the output\n            image, turning on this parameter will scale the mask to the\n            output image\u2019s resolution."], "extent": [2314, 2498]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If this node is changing constantly, and the mask is not, it\n            is somewhat faster to put a Scale COP down to do the resize\n            for the mask image. Otherwise, the scale will occur every\n            time this node cooks."], "extent": [2498, 2748]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Invert Mask"], "extent": [2748, 2769], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Inverts the mask so that all fully 'masked' portions become\n            unmasked. This saves you from inserting an Invert COP after\n            the node with the mask."], "extent": [2769, 2949]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Scope"], "extent": [484, 501], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Plane Scope"], "extent": [501, 523], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Specifies the scope for both the RGB components of Color,\n            Alpha, and other planes. The (C)RGBA mask only affects Color\n            components and Alpha. 'C' will toggle all the RGB\n            components."], "extent": [523, 753]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["For planes other than Color and Alpha, the plane name (plus\n            component, if applicable) should be specified in the string\n            field. The pulldown menu can be used to select planes or\n            components present in this node."], "extent": [753, 1012]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["A plane is specified by its name. A component is specified\n            by both its plane and component name. The '*' wildcard may\n            be used to scope all extra planes. Any number of planes or\n            components can be specified, separated by spaces."], "extent": [1012, 1288]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Examples:"], "extent": [1288, 1311]}, {"lang": null, "type": "pre", "indent": 12, "text": ["\n            P\n            N.x N.y\n            P N Pz\n            "], "extent": [1311, 1396]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 4, "text": ["Frame Scope"], "extent": [1396, 1419], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Frame Scope"], "extent": [1419, 1441], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["Allows scoping of specific frames in the frame range. This\n            is in addition to the plane scope (so a plane at a certain\n            frame must be both plane scoped and frame scoped to be\n            modified)."], "extent": [1441, 1674]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["All Frames"], "extent": [1674, 1698], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["All frames are scoped."], "extent": [1698, 1737]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Inside Range"], "extent": [1737, 1763], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["All frames inside a subrange are scoped."], "extent": [1763, 1820]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Outside Range"], "extent": [1820, 1847], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["All frames outside a subrange are scoped."], "extent": [1847, 1905]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Even Frames"], "extent": [1905, 1930], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Even numbered frames are scoped."], "extent": [1930, 1979]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Odd Frames"], "extent": [1979, 2003], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["Odd numbered frames are scoped."], "extent": [2003, 2051]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 12, "text": ["Specific Frames"], "extent": [2051, 2080], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 16, "text": ["A user-defined list of frames are scoped."], "extent": [2080, 2138]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Frame Range"], "extent": [2138, 2159], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["For Inside/Outside range, this parameter specifies the\n            subrange of the sequence to scope (or unscope). This can be\n            edited in Timeline viewer mode (", {"keys": ["Ctrl", "2"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " in viewer)."], "extent": [2201, 2409]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/frange1 /frange2"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Frame Dropoff"], "extent": [2409, 2432], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["For Inside/Outside Range, this parameter specifies certain\n            number of frames before and after to slowly ramp up to\n            scoped. The operation will be blended with its input to\n            'ease in' or 'ease out' the scoping effect over a number of\n            frames. This can be edited in Timeline viewer mode\n            (", {"keys": ["Ctrl", "2"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " in viewer)."], "extent": [2478, 2857]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/fdropoff1 /fdropoff2"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Non-scoped Effect"], "extent": [2857, 2884], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["For unscoped frames, this sets the blend factor between the\n            input and modified images. Normally this is zero (use the\n            input image). By setting this to a non-zero value, you can\n            make unscoped frames be 'slightly' unscoped. The value can\n            vary between 0 (unscoped) and 1 (scoped)."], "extent": [2918, 3256]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/foutside"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Frame List"], "extent": [3256, 3276], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["The frame list for 'Specific Frames'. Frame numbers should\n            be separated by spaces."], "extent": [3307, 3414]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"channels": "/flist"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 8, "text": ["Automatically Adjust for Length Changes"], "extent": [3414, 3463], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": ["If the sequence range changes, enabling this parameter will\n            adjust the subrange and frame dropoff lengths to fit the new\n            range."], "extent": [3463, 3627]}], "container": true, "role": "item"}], "container": true}]}], "text": "Parameters"}, {"level": 1, "id": "locals", "container": true, "type": "locals_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [7193, 7201], "body": [{"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["L"], "extent": [26, 29], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Sequence length"], "extent": [29, 49]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["S"], "extent": [49, 52], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Start of sequence"], "extent": [52, 74]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["E"], "extent": [74, 77], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["End of sequence"], "extent": [77, 97]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["IL"], "extent": [97, 101], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Input sequence length"], "extent": [101, 127]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["SR"], "extent": [127, 131], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Sequence frame rate"], "extent": [131, 155]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["NP"], "extent": [155, 159], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Number of planes in sequence"], "extent": [159, 192]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["W,H"], "extent": [192, 197], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Width and height of image"], "extent": [197, 227]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["I"], "extent": [227, 230], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Image index (0 at start frame)"], "extent": [230, 265]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["IT"], "extent": [265, 269], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Image time (0 at start frame)"], "extent": [269, 303]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["AI"], "extent": [303, 307], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Current plane array index"], "extent": [307, 337]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["PI"], "extent": [337, 341], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Current plane index"], "extent": [341, 365]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["PC"], "extent": [365, 369], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Num of channels in current plane"], "extent": [369, 406]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CXRES"], "extent": [406, 413], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project X resolution"], "extent": [413, 448]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CYRES"], "extent": [448, 455], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project Y resolution"], "extent": [455, 490]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CPIXA"], "extent": [490, 497], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project pixel aspect ratio"], "extent": [497, 538]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CDEPTH"], "extent": [538, 546], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project raster depth"], "extent": [546, 581]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CBP"], "extent": [581, 586], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project black point"], "extent": [586, 620]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["CWP"], "extent": [620, 625], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Composite Project white point"], "extent": [625, 659]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "text": "Locals"}, {"level": 1, "id": "related", "container": true, "type": "related_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [7227, 7236], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/bump", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/bump.html"}], "extent": [7236, 7259]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/dof", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/dof.html"}], "extent": [7259, 7281]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/emboss", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/emboss.html"}], "extent": [7281, 7306]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/fog", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/fog.html"}], "extent": [7306, 7329]}], "container": true}], "text": "Related"}], "title": ["Lighting"], "summary": ["Adds a light to the image."], "included": ["/composite/_old_cops_deprecated", "/nodes/cop2/localvars", "/nodes/cop2/maskparms", "/nodes/cop2/pixelparms", "/nodes/cop2/vexnode"]}